WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.354
Once upon a time there lived a beautiful hart.

2
00:00:04.355 --> 00:00:08.220
The hart was tall, proud, and graceful.

3
00:00:08.221 --> 00:00:13.658
But his most outstanding feature was his antlers.

4
00:00:13.659 --> 00:00:17.527
Every day the hart came to drink from the river.

5
00:00:17.528 --> 00:00:24.956
And every day, the hart would admire his reflection in the water.

6
00:00:24.957 --> 00:00:29.242
"Just look!" the hart exclaimed.

7
00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:33.061
"Look at these magnificent antlers!

8
00:00:33.062 --> 00:00:40.795
No one has such beautiful antlers as I!" he boasted.

9
00:00:40.796 --> 00:00:45.328
The hart stood and admired his antlers for a long time.

10
00:00:45.329 --> 00:00:49.434
No one was allowed to touch his precious antlers.

11
00:00:49.435 --> 00:00:55.591
Not even little birds taking a little break!

12
00:00:55.592 --> 00:01:00.367
"Shoo! Shoo!" he would swing his legs at the bird.

13
00:01:00.368 --> 00:01:06.128
"How dare you sit on my beautiful antlers!" he scolded.

14
00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:10.336
The hart looked to make sure his antlers were okay.

15
00:01:10.337 --> 00:01:15.950
"Oh!" he suddenly cried.

16
00:01:15.951 --> 00:01:18.830
The hart lifted his leg higher.

17
00:01:18.831 --> 00:01:21.529
"What a shame!" he moaned.

18
00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:27.913
"These legs are not worthy to hold my great antlers!" The hart frowned.

19
00:01:27.914 --> 00:01:32.868
"I wish my legs were more beautiful!"

20
00:01:32.869 --> 00:01:38.481
The hart was so distressed that he did not know he was being watched.

21
00:01:38.482 --> 00:01:41.501
"Look at those magnificent antlers!"

22
00:01:41.502 --> 00:01:44.524
the hunter was thinking to himself.

23
00:01:44.525 --> 00:01:48.421
The hunter slowly took out his arrow.

24
00:01:48.422 --> 00:01:54.494
He aimed carefully at the hart.

25
00:01:54.495 --> 00:01:57.390
The arrow flew but missed the hart. At

26
00:01:57.391 --> 00:02:02.064
that moment the hart turned and saw the hunter. "Oh!

27
00:02:02.065 --> 00:02:08.929
Oh!" he cried as he quickly ran away. The

28
00:02:08.930 --> 00:02:12.449
hart nimbly jumped over fallen trees. His

29
00:02:12.450 --> 00:02:16.266
legs gracefully carried him through the forest. The

30
00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:20.502
hunter could not keep up with the hart. The

31
00:02:20.503 --> 00:02:23.708
hart ran as swift as the wind. No

32
00:02:23.709 --> 00:02:28.536
one, not even the birds, were as fast as the hart. After

33
00:02:28.537 --> 00:02:33.088
some time, he turned around to look for the hunter. The

34
00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:38.156
hunter was nowhere to be seen. The

35
00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:41.678
hart laughed with relief and joy. But

36
00:02:41.679 --> 00:02:44.918
not for long! Smash !

37
00:02:44.919 --> 00:02:48.344
The hart was not watching where he was going.

38
00:02:48.345 --> 00:02:56.114
His great antlers got stuck in some branches.

39
00:02:56.115 --> 00:02:59.074
The hart tried to free himself.

40
00:02:59.075 --> 00:03:04.349
But no matter which way he turned, his antlers would not budge.

41
00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:12.840
"Oh, why are you so big and grand?" he shouted at his antlers.

42
00:03:12.841 --> 00:03:17.877
Meanwhile, the hunter was able to catch up with the hart.

43
00:03:17.878 --> 00:03:20.701
The hart looked down at his legs.

44
00:03:20.702 --> 00:03:30.333
"Even though you are not as beautiful as my antlers," he said, "you carried me fast and far!

45
00:03:30.334 --> 00:03:44.308
Oh, how we despise what is most useful to us!" the hart cried with regret.

